OL,3,GNEWSAMisspelt signs feature Bolton
OL,4,Avillage and Swiss firm
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents in a suburb in Derbyshire
OL,7,Fhave been left bemused by misspelt road
OL,8,Fsigns that appear to direct people to a
OL,9,Fvillage in Bolton and a Swiss
OL,10,Fproduction company based in Zurich.
OL,12,FThe temporary signs near the A38 were
OL,13,Fintended to direct traffic to nearby
OL,14,FHilton and Egginton but instead say
OL,15,F"Egerton" and "Hillton".
OL,17,FSouth Derbyshire district councillor
OL,18,FGrahame Andrew said it was the second
OL,19,Ftime National Highways had made the
OL,20,Ferror, as it had also happened in
OL,21,FOctober 2025.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,363,360,200,160,0,100
